# Error Handling

## Result type (`ijs-error-lib`)
```kotlin
sealed class Result<out T> {
    object Loading : Result<Nothing>()
    data class Success<T>(val data: T) : Result<T>()
    data class Error(val exception: Throwable? = null, val message: String? = null) : Result<Nothing>()
}
```

## In repositories — wrap API calls
```kotlin
try {
    val response = remoteDataSource.getData(token)
    emit(Result.Success(mapper.mapToDomain(response.data)))
} catch (e: Exception) {
    emit(Result.Error(e, ApiErrorHandler.extractMessage(e)))
}
```

## In ViewModels — handle all three states
```kotlin
when (result) {
    is Result.Loading -> updateState { copy(isLoading = true, error = null) }
    is Result.Success -> updateState { copy(isLoading = false, data = result.data) }
    is Result.Error -> {
        updateState { copy(isLoading = false, error = result.message) }
        sendEffect(Effect.ShowSnackbar(result.message ?: "Something went wrong"))
    }
}
```

## Rules
- Use `com.indusjs.error.result.Result`, NOT `kotlin.Result`
- Use `ApiErrorHandler.extractMessage(e)` for user-friendly error messages
- 401 errors trigger `AuthenticationManager` logout flow automatically
- Always clear `error` state when starting a new load (`error = null`)
